  _signatureText: At three quarters, half and a quarter of its health it dives under the ground. A crack line runs round your towers to the tower that hurt it most; it breaks out beside it and throws that tower. The tower lands tilted, loses 40% of its health and stays silent for a few seconds, but it is not destroyed. It takes quicksand as a shortcut, climbs over rocks and onto gates, and can hide in a pool for a few seconds.
  _telegraphText: The crack glows warm orange and runs ahead of it, the ground rumbles louder as it comes up, and the tower it is after gets a pulsing red ring three seconds before it breaks out.
  _counterText: 'Spread your damage over several towers, so no single tower draws it. Sell or move the ringed tower in time, or put a mine on the crack line: a mine that goes off while it burrows leaves it stunned on the surface. Below a quarter it moves faster and its cracks send up Skitters.'
